; THE SAME FACTORIAL, DECLARED FINITE — so it carries a BOUND.
;
; `examples/big/fact.oro` is this program with `(int 0 +inf)`. The difference
; between the two is SEMANTIC and it is the whole of the difference: this one
; says the value stays under 2^1300 and the compiler enforces that, and the
; other says there is no upper bound at all.
;
; WHICH STORAGE EACH GETS IS NOT IN THIS FILE, and that separation was got wrong
; at first. A finite range used to SELECT fixed limbs and `+inf` used to select
; the host's own bignum, so the shape of a declaration chose a representation —
; and on V8 that cost 75x for the same computation. A range is a fact about the
; program, true on every target; the storage is a target declaration, exactly as
; `int-repr` decides one rung down that `(int 0 255)` is a `[]byte` on Go and a
; `short[]` on the JVM because the JVM's byte is signed.
;
; So today Go, JavaScript and Java store this in their own bignum and windows
; stores it in 55 base-2^24 limbs, because it ships no bignum. Ask for the other
; one with `-big-repr=limbs`, which is how the alternative gets measured before
; a target file is changed to prefer it (gauntlet/results/bigrepr-2026-09-03.md).
;
; 200! is 375 digits, about 1,246 bits, so 52 base-2^24 limbs are significant.
; `(pow 2 1300)` names a comfortable 55.
;
; WHAT HAPPENS IF THE BOUND IS TOO SMALL is the question the declaration has to
; answer, and the answer is a TRAP — on BOTH representations, at the same value.
; A fixed width has no choice: it would otherwise truncate. The host's bignum is
; exact whatever the declaration says, so it is checked explicitly, or selecting
; a representation would change which programs are legal. That is ADR 0009's
; rule at the representation boundary.
;
; The bound is enforced at its BIT LENGTH, so `(pow 2 1300)` admits everything
; under 2^1301 — slack of less than a factor of two, and what makes the check
; O(1) on the host rung and free on the limb rung, where it falls out of the
; carry.

(export fact-limbs)

(sig fact-limbs ((n (int 0 200))) (int 0 (pow 2 1300)))

(def fact-limbs (fn (n)
  (loop ((acc 1) (i 2))
    (> i n)  acc
    else     (again (* acc i) (+ i 1)))))
